___NOTES___

Adwize Data Quality Monitor GTM Tag Template (Server-Side)
===========================================================

This tag captures events processed by a server-side Google Tag Manager
container and forwards them to the Adwize API for quality monitoring
and alerting.

Setup:
1. Import this template into your server-side GTM container
   (Templates > Tag Templates > New > Import)
2. Create a new tag using this template (Tags > New > select "Adwize")
3. Enter your API key from the Adwize dashboard (Settings > API Keys)
4. Add a trigger (typically "All Events" on the server container)
5. Preview to verify events are forwarded
6. Publish your container

Differences vs. the web (client-side) template:
- Uses getEventData/getAllEventData instead of copyFromDataLayer
- Uses sendHttpRequest (POST with JSON body + API key header) instead
  of sendPixel (GET with query-string payload)
- Runs in a SERVER container context
- No access to the browser dataLayer or the current page URL DOM; the
  page URL is read from the incoming event's page_location property

Tests:
The template includes 9 unit tests covering all trigger modes, edge
cases, request construction, and failure handling. After importing, go
to the template editor > Tests tab and click "Run Tests" to validate.

